-- title:
--   Transversal primes in a regular local ring of dimension ≤ 2
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring that is a regular local ring in Mathlib's sense, and suppose its Krull dimension satisfies $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} R \le 2$ (the inequality being taken in $\mathbb{N}^\infty$ with a bottom element adjoined). Let $P$ and $Q$ be prime ideals of $R$, each distinct from the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $R$, such that $P \vee Q = \mathfrak m$, i.e. the ideal generated by $P$ and $Q$ is the whole maximal ideal. Let $\pi \in R$ be nonzero and assume $P \cap Q = (\pi)$, the ideal generated by the single element $\pi$. The conclusion asserts the existence of elements $u, v \in R$ and a unit $c \in R^\times$ such that $P = (u)$, $Q = (v)$, and $u v = c\pi$ in $R$ (the unit being coerced to $R$). Thus both primes are principal and the product of their generators is the given generator of the intersection, up to a unit; no nonvanishing assertion about $u$ or $v$ is part of the stated conclusion, although it follows from $\pi \ne 0$.
--
--   This is the local algebra behind two transversal branches through the closed point of a regular two-dimensional local ring: if their intersection is principal, each branch is itself cut out by a single equation, and the two equations multiply to the generator of the intersection up to a unit. It is used in the construction of étale crossing charts on a two-chart model of the modular curve $X_1(p)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsRegularLocalRing_exists_span_singleton_eq_and_span_singleton_eq_and_mul_eq_of_sup_eq_maximalIdeal_of_inf_eq_span_singleton.lean

